This is something that's passed to the mirt.model() builder, so when implemented you could use item names too. So this:

 specific <- "S1 = 7,9,10,11,13,15,17,18,21,22,24,27,31
              S2 = 1,3,6,8,16,29,32
              S3 = 2,4,5,12,14,19,20,23,25,26,28,30"

could also be specified as

 specific <- "S1 = item7, item9,...
              S2 = item1,item3,...
              S3 = item2, item4, ..."

It's just a matter of preference.

Phil

