I don't believe this is possible to do in the current implementation of mixedmirt() as the slopes are assumed to be equal across the person/clusters (if they are unequal, this gets into DIF territory). I haven't read that paper though, so perhaps this is something different. Note that for these types of random effects models it's nearly always better to use dedicated MCMC estimators as they become unstable and high-dimensional quite quickly (e.g., see brms or stan for implementation). HTH.

