Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/mirt-package/c/KWkkRfaZkP8/m/3uH-fNXcAwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi Adon,

I don't know if you'll have luck finding closed form solutions to this problem, but you can always numerically integrate across your p.d.f. for theta instead. Something like the following would work to compute the expected first and second moments (mean/var):

######

pop1.vals <- rnorm(1000)
a <- matrix(rlnorm(20,.2,.3)) ## discrim vals
d <- rnorm(20) ## diff vals
dat <- simdata(a, d, Theta = pop1.vals, itemtype = '2PL') ## create data

mod <- mirt(dat)

E <- function(theta, pdf, ...)
    expected.test(mod, Theta=theta) * pdf(theta, ...)

VAR <- function(theta, pdf, E, ...)
    (expected.test(mod, Theta=theta) - E)^2 * pdf(theta, ...)

# expected total score
exp <- integrate(E, lower = -Inf, upper=Inf, pdf=dnorm)
exp

# expected variance of total scores
expv <- integrate(VAR, lower = -Inf, upper=Inf, pdf=dnorm, E=exp$value)
expv
expv$value |> sqrt() # standard deviation

# different pdf
exp <- integrate(E, lower = -Inf, upper=Inf, pdf=dnorm, mean=-.25)
exp
expv <- integrate(VAR, lower = -Inf, upper=Inf, pdf=dnorm, E=exp$value, mean=-.25)
expv
expv$value |> sqrt() # standard deviation
####

HTH.

Phil

