Hello Phil,

I have a question regarding using a free-baseline anchor approach to detect DIF for two booklets. I'm working on two booklets that used matrix sampling. So these two booklets only shared half of the items, and the other half of the items are unique for each of the booklets.

When I run the free-baseline anchor approach for each booklet, I can have item parameter estimates for each item within that booklet. However, the items shared by both booklets will have different parameter estimates since two groups of students responded.

Then I tried to use the free-baseline anchor approach for two-booklet data together. However, the models were not convergent when I used the "add" scheme to detect DIF at the last step, it always had the warning "EM cycles terminated after 500 iterations".

Could you please give me some advice on how to cope with the warning when I want to analyze two booklets together? And if I analyze each booklet separately, how to deal with different item parameter estimates for the same items because of the sample difference?

I really appreciate your help and your advice!

Best,
Yiqi

